---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---

<SiteLayout title="Development | ArcadeDuck" description="ArcadeDuck's current priorities, upcoming hardware milestones, and release process.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Development</p>
    <h1>Where ArcadeDuck goes next</h1>
    <p class="page-description">Hardware milestones guide development. Testing and compatibility reports determine when the next one is ready.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="systems-status-section">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Current Focus</p><h2>System 12 stabilization</h2></div>
      <p>System 12 support has been added. Community testing, compatibility reports, control issues, and regressions are the current priority.</p>
    </div>
    <p>For the complete hardware lineup and current support status, see <a href={`${base}systems/`}>Systems</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="systems-status-section">
    <div class="systems-group-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Upcoming Milestones</p><h2>System 10, System 573, and Twinkle</h2></div>
      <p>These hardware families remain in development. Research and testing can change their release order; there are no promised dates.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="systems-note">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Release Process</p><h2>Build. Test. Stabilize. Repeat.</h2></div>
    <p>Implement enough hardware for meaningful testing, release it to users and cabinets, and work through reports before moving to the next platform. Arcade hardware has a habit of turning one simple subsystem into three weeks of reverse engineering.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="systems-note">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The Long-Term Plan</p><h2>Keep going until there is nothing left to implement.</h2></div>
    <p>The first public release was September 19, 2026. The plan is to keep expanding PlayStation-derived arcade support until I either run out of hardware or remaining brain cells.</p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
